 {:value "357860"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016828"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/284"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Sabre, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2167"} "Grand Palais, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2011283"} "34 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The big question coming in was if Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/118239"} "Áron Szilágyi"] " would win his fourth consecutive gold medal in the event. He was seeded only #6 and the question was answered early, as he lost his first match to the #27 seeded Canadian, " [:a {:href "/athletes/151878"} "Farès Arfa"] ". With Szilágyi out, the focus settled on the #1 seed, Egyptian " [:a {:href "/athletes/1303162"} "Ziad El-Sissy"] ", and the second seed, Georgia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/134088"} "Sandro Bazadze"] ". Bazadze was world ranked #1 early in 2024, but he fared no better than Szilágyi, losing in the round of 16 to El-Sissy’s teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/133563"} "Mohamed Amer"] ", 15-14."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Upsets continued as El-Sissy made it to the semi-finals but then lost to Tunisian " [:a {:href "/athletes/136104"} "Fares Ferjani"] ", the 13th seed. In the other half, Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/145003"} "Oh Sang-Uk"] " defeated Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/127221"} "Luigi Samele"] " to advance to the final. Oh was the 2019 World Champion and favored over the unknown Ferjani, and he won gold relatively easily, 15-11. This was the fifth gold medal for Korea in men’s fencing, moving them to sixth all-time among NOCs."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was the first Olympic fencing medal by a Tunisian man, although " [:a {:href "/athletes/118185"} "Inès Boubakri"] " won bronze in the 2016 women’s individual foil. Tunisia’s previous best finish in this event had been 22nd by Ferjani at Tokyo 2020. Their previous best finish in a men’s individual fencing event was 17th by " [:a {:href "/athletes/126072"} "Mohamed Samandi"] " in 2012 individual foil. Luigi Samele took the bronze medal, defeating El-Sissy in the bronze medal match, 15-12."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145003"} "Oh Sang-Uk"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "12"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136104"} "Fares Ferjani"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUN.png"}] "TUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/127221"} "Luigi Samele"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/1303162"} "Ziad El-Sissy"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/EGY"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :s